{"title": "GI Ego1, global-shutter module", "parts": {"lead": "<p class=lead>A GI Ego1 platform from GiLabs that appears to carry a global-shutter camera module, with a 200 Hz IMU. The label comes from the solved readout, not from a maker&#x27;s statement.</p><div class=chips><span class=chip>Appears global shutter</span><span class=chip>Stereo</span><span class=chip>200 Hz IMU</span><span class=chip>CC BY-NC 4.0</span></div>", "glance": "<div class=band><figure class=demo><video src=\"/media/sensors/gi-ego1-gs-module/demo.mp4\" poster=\"/media/sensors/gi-ego1-gs-module/demo.jpg\" autoplay muted loop playsinline controls preload=metadata></video><figcaption>The 3D scene MVIS recovered from this recording.</figcaption></figure><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=tiles><div><span>Reprojection median</span><b>0.20<small> px</small></b></div><div><span>cam0–cam1 baseline</span><b>61.9<small> mm</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 td</span><b>+26.93<small> ms</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 lever arm</span><b>32.9<small> mm</small></b></div></div></div></div>", "process": "<p>The solved path of the rig around the board. Press Play or drag the bar to follow the calibration. Camera images are left out to keep the page small.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=procplot id=\"proc0\"></div><div class=\"mvis-progress\" data-plot=\"proc0\"><button type=button>▶ Play</button><select class=\"mvis-progress-cam\" aria-label=\"Camera shown\"><option value=\"0\">cam0</option><option value=\"1\">cam1</option></select><input type=range min=0 max=599 value=599 step=1 aria-label=\"Calibration progress\"><span class=\"mvis-progress-label\">Loading</span></div></div>", "map": "<p>Solved positions and orientations, to scale in the IMU frame. Drag sideways to orbit. Tap a sensor for its values.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div>", "hardware": "<div class=scroll><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Shutter</td><td>Appears global: solved readout −1.5 and −0.6 ms, against about −26 ms on rolling-shutter units</td><td><span class=chip>Measured</span></td></tr><tr><td>Cameras</td><td>2 × 1920×1080 at about 30 fps</td><td><span class=chip>Measured</span></td></tr><tr><td>IMU rate</td><td>200.8 Hz in this recording</td><td><span class=chip>Measured</span></td></tr><tr><td>Sensor part numbers</td><td>Not published</td><td><span class=chip>Unknown</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Maker's specs from <a href=\"https://www.gilabs.xyz/blog/ego1\">www.gilabs.xyz/blog/ego1</a>, checked 2026-10-15.</p>", "dataset": "<div class=two><div class=scroll><table><tbody><tr><td>Recording</td><td>2026-07-24, 30.1 s</td></tr><tr><td>Format</td><td>MCAP, H.265, 61 MB</td></tr><tr><td>Frames kept at decode</td><td>cam0 876 of 900, cam1 876 of 900</td></tr><tr><td>Board</td><td>AprilGrid 6×6, tag 35.2 mm, spacing 0.3</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>CC BY-NC 4.0, for the data and for this page&#x27;s clip and figures; commercial use by request</td></tr><tr><td>Hosted</td><td><a href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/calibench-vi/datasets/tree/main/gilabs-examples/\">Calibench, gilabs-examples/</a> (access on request)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div><svg class=board viewBox=\"-5.3 -5.3 274.6 295.7\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"AprilGrid layout to scale\"><rect x=\"0.00\" y=\"0.00\" width=\"35.2\" height=\"35.2\"/><rect x=\"45.76\" y=\"0.00\" width=\"35.2\" height=\"35.2\"/><rect x=\"91.52\" y=\"0.00\" width=\"35